WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.008
[traffic noise]

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:12.012
[Jason]<i> Well, let's figure out who's </i>
<i>sitting what on Sunday and Tuesday.</i>

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:15.265
We've got Queens, which is new, at 4.7,

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:16.892
-so I guess we can sit Queens.
-Okay.

00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:19.937
Christine, you can sit your own listing
on Hollywood, I guess.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.273
I'm gonna do Doheny.
Brett, which one are you doing?

00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:24.191
Crescent.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:25.567
-Mary?
-I could do one Sunday.

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:28.445
-You wanna sit Temecula for a backup?
-Yeah, that works.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:30.364
We don't do this often, as you know,

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:34.618
but we are bringing another girl
on to the brokerage.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.119
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:39.122
She's gonna be here in a few minutes,
so I wanted you guys to be aware.

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:40.249
-From where?
-Chrishell.

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:41.875
She was at-- Crishell.

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:43.168
-Chrishell?
-With a K?

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:44.086
Katrell?

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.421
Yeah, I can tell how well
this is going to go.

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:49.091
-No, we're open, of course!
-I've heard really good things.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.301
She does serious business.
She's got a lot of clients.

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:54.137
Her personality, you think she'll
get along well with everybody?

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:57.391
Yeah, I wouldn't bring anybody on that,
I didn't think would gel with all of us.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:59.810
-Even Christine might like her.
-Watch out.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:00.852
Where's she gonna sit?

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:02.896
She can sit on the floor
until she proves herself.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.147
Yeah. Right.

00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:06.233
-Be nice, girls, be nice.
-Always!

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:08.569
Seriously, she's gonna be
naturally intimidated.

00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:11.738
-So do your best to--
-Christine, you heard that?

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:13.699
Yeah, just be nice when she comes in.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:15.409
-How do you say her name?
-Chrishell.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:17.786
Chrishell. Okay. Cool.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:19.705
<i>♪ Let's get to work ♪</i>

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:22.833
I'm Jason Oppenheim,
and this is my twin brother Brett.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.628
<i>Together we built and own</i>
<i>the Oppenheim Group brokerage here.</i>

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:30.549
<i>We are far and away the number one</i>
<i>real estate team, in West Hollywood.</i>

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.218
<i>We sell a quarter billion dollars a year.</i>

00:01:33.302 --> 00:01:34.845
<i>Anyone who's buying or selling,</i>

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.598
<i>in the Sunset Strip</i>
<i>and the Hollywood Hills calls us.</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:39.182
♪ <i>Let's get to work </i>♪

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:43.895
♪ <i>Let's get to work </i>♪

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.858
It may be our name on the door,
but behind those doors,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.777
is all of the kick ass women,
that make this brokerage what it is.

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:57.951
[Christine] <i>I am the go-to agent, when it </i>
<i>comes to selling these high-end homes.</i>

00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:02.789
<i>Luxury, glamour, style is my thing,</i>
<i>and that's why my clients come to me.</i>

00:02:02.873 --> 00:02:05.292
You made the right choice.
This house is amazing.

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:11.048
[Mary] <i>I bust my ass. I'm always on call.</i>

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.592
<i>I was one of the first people, </i>
<i>to start at the Oppenheim Group.</i>

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:16.470
<i>Jason, he says he does about 20% growth.</i>

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:18.513
I'm like, "Cool.
I'll do about 40% growth every year."

00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:20.265
This is super fresh.

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:22.100
<i>♪ Baby, I'm the real thing ♪</i>

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:26.063
[Maya] 
<i>I'm not afraid to get down and dirty.</i>

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.023
<i>It's honestly not always glamorous.</i>

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:29.524
It's just part of the business.

00:02:29.608 --> 00:02:33.070
<i>You have to have a vision, and if you </i>
<i>do a nice job</i> <i>with nice finishes,</i>

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.530
<i>you're gonna actually</i>
<i>make a million-dollar profit.</i>

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.660
[Heather] 
<i>I have great international connections.</i>

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:42.079
The real estate business 
is all about building relationships.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.830
[speaking foreign language]

00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:47.250
If this doesn't sell the house,
I don't know what will.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.003
♪ Baby, I'm the real thing ♪

00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:55.592
[Chrishell] <i>My favorite part </i>
<i>of being a real estate agent</i>

00:02:55.676 --> 00:02:57.386
<i>is, I feel like I'm a matchmaker.</i>

00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:58.929
It's kind of like falling in love.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:02.599
<i>I have that passion for working</i>
<i>with first-time homeowners.</i>

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:06.645
My job is to take the stress on,
and let you enjoy the process.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:08.897
[woman] 
Mm-hmm. It's definitely breathtaking.

00:03:09.481 --> 00:03:10.649
Cheers to that!

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:13.527
-We're a bad-ass crew to hang out with.
-Yeah, you have to have thick skin.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.737
I thought we could work together,
but clearly we can't.

00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:17.864
When was the last time you were
in a relationship?

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:19.199
Like, a proper relationship?

00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:21.827
-You were throwing me under the bus.
-But you could've owned up to it.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.037
Do you have, like, dementia? I don't know.

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:26.748
[Mary] <i>We're always juggling a lot.</i>

00:03:26.832 --> 00:03:29.918
<i>But at the end of the day,</i>
<i>our clients always come first.</i>

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:31.837
Welcome to your dream home, guys.

00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:45.350
♪ <i>Baby, I'm the real thing </i>♪

00:03:50.981 --> 00:03:54.609
Heather. Heather, just make sure
your offer's the first one in.

00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.153
-Okay. All right.
-[Jason] All right.

00:03:56.278 --> 00:03:57.946
-[Heather] Thanks, guys.
-[man]<i> I trust you.</i>

00:03:58.029 --> 00:03:59.322
[Heather] Perfect, I have your email...

00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:01.533
[Jason] Listen, yes, of course
you can show both of those.

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.577
[Christine] Um, we can get going with it,
'cause it's gonna...

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.830
Hey, bro, did you ever get a call
from those potential buyers?

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.374
Hi, this is Christine Quinn
from the Oppenheim Group. How are you?

00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:12.210
Listen, I'm here with an associate
of mine. Actually, she...

00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:14.337
-Do you have the plans for Doheny?
-Yeah.

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:17.340
So let me look at it and I'll
just call you back, okay?

00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:20.093
Cool, awesome. All right. Bye.

00:04:21.219 --> 00:04:23.054
-[Jason] Hey, Mary.
-Hey, babe.

00:04:23.138 --> 00:04:25.390
-Hey.
-How did the showing go?

00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:26.933
Amazing!

00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:29.478
-[Christine] Go on.
-So, they like everything.

00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:34.065
We got the offer in higher
than we expected. Three-five-fifty.

00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:35.025
It's higher, so...

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.818
Our clients will take that.
Good, nice work.

00:04:36.902 --> 00:04:38.904
-I want it in writing. When are we--
-We got it.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:41.448
-In writing? Okay, good.
-Yeah, she just sent it through.

00:04:41.531 --> 00:04:42.824
You want to call them together or...

00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:45.952
I mean, honestly, for 12 thousand, it's--
I think it's a steal.

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:49.080
Hey, Natalie.
So I've got Jason here with me.

00:04:49.164 --> 00:04:49.998
Hey, Natalie.

00:04:50.081 --> 00:04:53.668
The good news is Mary got them to step up
to the three-five-fifty.

00:04:53.752 --> 00:04:55.796
So, uh, I hope we have a deal.

00:04:57.506 --> 00:04:59.090
<i>-Yeah, we have a deal.</i>
-[Jason chuckles]

00:04:59.174 --> 00:05:00.133
-Fantastic!
-[Jason] Okay.

00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:02.511
-All right, talk soon Natalie.
-[Mary] Our pleasure.

00:05:02.594 --> 00:05:04.137
<i>-Bye-bye.</i>
-Bye.

00:05:04.221 --> 00:05:05.263
Cool?

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:11.895
-Hello.
-Hi.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.647
-Wow. Hi.
-Good to meet you.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.566
You too. Good to see you. Hi.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.693
[Jason] Girls, this is Chrishell,
the girl I told you about.

00:05:18.777 --> 00:05:21.613
Yeah, we have a new girl in the office
and guess what?

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:24.157
She's a pretty girl. Shocking.

00:05:24.241 --> 00:05:25.742
-Hi.
-Good to see you.

00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:27.035
Good to see you.

00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:28.203
I came bearing gifts.

00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:30.288
Why would I want a-- Nico!

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:32.749
You said there were dogs in the office.
Hi!

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:34.668
[Christine] 
<i>My first impression of Chrishell</i>

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.878
<i>is that she's used to being a kiss-ass,</i>

00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:39.548
and she was always that girl in school
that asked for extra credit.

00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:42.884
That'll be interesting to see how she gets
along with everybody, AKA me.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.595
-Let me introduce you to some people.
-Okay.

00:05:45.679 --> 00:05:47.514
Girls. Chrishell.

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:48.431
Hi, guys.

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:51.101
-Hi, I'm Maya.
-Hi, Maya, Chrishell. Nice to meet you.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.020
First day on a new job is really scary.

00:05:54.104 --> 00:05:57.065
They're all so beautiful,
that was the first thing I noticed.

00:05:57.148 --> 00:05:58.692
I know they're so successful.

00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:00.944
I was a little intimidated,
I'm not gonna lie.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.612
It kind of felt like high school..

00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:04.364
Beautiful, hi, nice to meet you.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:08.952
I mean, whether is was the Ann Taylor,
like, Driving Ms. Daisy dress--

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:12.038
I don't know, I think she's,
like, really nice.

00:06:12.122 --> 00:06:14.791
I just want to work
on her style a little bit.

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.544
-Is it welcome, Chris-- Chrishell?
-Chrishell.

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:18.837
-Yes.
-Chrishell, okay.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.840
I moved from Kentucky to Los Angeles
to be an actress,

00:06:21.923 --> 00:06:24.843
<i>and then I got a job on a soap opera,</i>
<i>on </i>All My Children.

00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:27.262
<i>But what happens with acting </i>
<i>is there's a lot of downtime.</i>

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:30.098
And I was like, "You know, I have 
the time. I've always wanted to do it."

00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:31.683
So I went and got my license,

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:35.312
and now it's kind of nice, because 
something that I did in my off time,

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.188
I've found is a real passion of mine.

00:06:37.272 --> 00:06:39.608
Try to remember, how nervous
you guys were meeting everybody,

00:06:39.691 --> 00:06:40.901
the first time you came in.

00:06:40.984 --> 00:06:43.904
-You've been married for how long?
-In October, it'll be one year.

00:06:43.987 --> 00:06:45.655
-But we've been together five years.
-Ooh.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.950
So my husband is Justin Hartley.
Maybe you've heard of him.

00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:50.660
He's on a show <i>This is Us.</i>

00:06:50.744 --> 00:06:51.661
I love him to death.

00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:55.040
We've been together five years,
but married almost one.

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:57.334
So do you live around the office?

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:59.461
-I'm actually in Sherman Oaks.
-Cool.

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:01.880
Any open houses north of Mulholland,
that's her.

00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:02.797
[laughs]

00:07:02.881 --> 00:07:04.883
-We need someone, yeah.
-We need someone there.

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:05.800
-[Jason] I know.
-I'd love to.

00:07:06.217 --> 00:07:09.262
You've got LA here. 
You've got the Hills, the Hollywood Hills.

00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:13.350
But then, over a big canyon behind
all of that, is the Valley,

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.143
and it's a little hotter,

00:07:15.226 --> 00:07:18.021
but the real estate, you get
a lot more for your money

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.940
and it's really residential.

00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:22.984
You don't have to have a reservation,
every time you wanna go to dinner,

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:24.986
and I personally think it's better.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.947
And the newest person
brings Starbucks, too.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.658
Okay. I've got it. I've got it. Okay.

00:07:29.741 --> 00:07:31.660
If you have 
any questions or anything, I mean,

00:07:31.743 --> 00:07:34.621
I think we'll all try to be nice. 
[chuckles]

00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:36.957
True, you have to watch out for her, but--
She can be...

00:07:37.582 --> 00:07:40.043
I'm just sitting here.
What are you talking about?

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:44.339
Maybe I'm a little cold,
but I've always been honest out the gate,

00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:47.092
and I think a lot of people aren't
necessarily honest,

00:07:47.175 --> 00:07:49.886
because they wanna tell people,
what they think they want to hear,

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.389
and that's not what I'm here for.
-Welcome to the team, Chrishell.

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:56.726
Thank you, guys, so much. I appreciate it.
I'm so excited to join, so thank you.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.354
[Chrishell]<i> There's obviously a lot </i>
<i>of nerves going into, you know,</i>

00:07:59.437 --> 00:08:01.815
being the new girl going into
such a tight-knit group.

00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:04.109
But I think it was a good start.

00:08:04.192 --> 00:08:05.652
<i>♪ Come to life </i>♪

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:12.033
[Mary] <i>This is like the house </i>
<i>that everyone's going to be talking about.</i>

00:08:12.117 --> 00:08:14.494
Oh, yeah, I'm already thinking about
what buyers I'm getting up here.

00:08:14.577 --> 00:08:17.497
[Davina] I know. I was just gonna say
that's what I want to do.

00:08:18.248 --> 00:08:20.000
It's an awesome location, this place.

00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:22.752
-I can't wait to see it.
-I wore the right shoes for this.

00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:24.713
Yeah, genius. Yeah.

00:08:28.383 --> 00:08:30.427
-Hey, guys.
-Hey, team.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.887
This is incredible.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.975
[Chrishell] Check out that view!

00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:39.060
-Right?
-Wow, this is amazing.

00:08:39.561 --> 00:08:41.688
This is a little different
than the two bedroom condos,

00:08:41.771 --> 00:08:43.565
I've been showing in the Valley.

00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:46.276
This is actually the biggest house
ever built, in the Hollywood Hills.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.319
<i>♪ Step back</i>
<i>Here comes the queen ♪</i>

00:08:48.403 --> 00:08:50.321
♪ <i>I'm in charge</i>
<i>Don't mess with me </i>♪

00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:52.949
[Jason] <i>This is the biggest listing</i>
<i>that we've ever had.</i>

00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:55.744
<i>When it's done,</i>
<i>it will be over 20,000 square feet.</i>

00:08:55.827 --> 00:08:59.205
<i>Five luxurious bedrooms</i>
<i>and nine bathrooms.</i>

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:00.915
-This is the master closet.
-Oh, wow.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:03.460
This is the closet?
I thought it was the master bedroom.

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.045
-It's a closet?
-This is a closet, yeah.

00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:06.046
[Chrishell chuckles]

00:09:06.129 --> 00:09:08.298
<i>♪ Just watch me now ♪</i>

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:11.009
<i>♪ Just watch me, just watch me</i>
<i>Just watch me now ♪</i>

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:14.512
[Brett]<i> Not only that, it has </i>
<i>a 15-car garage, four hot tubs,</i>

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:16.056
150-foot pool,

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:17.974
360-degree views from the rooftop deck,

00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:19.684
and an elevator,
that takes you up there.

00:09:19.768 --> 00:09:21.227
-Wow, look at that view.
-What?

00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:22.604
The view's gonna get even better.

00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:27.400
All four of these power lines are going
to be dropped, at a cost of over $400000.

00:09:27.484 --> 00:09:31.613
Ugh, this is so Marilyn up here.
Like, look at this breeze.

00:09:31.696 --> 00:09:33.364
This is actually where the television
comes up,

00:09:33.448 --> 00:09:37.077
so you can watch the 16-foot television
from the master bedroom.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.371
Okay, as much as I like looking
at a fake TV, can we please do the roof?

00:09:40.455 --> 00:09:41.915
-[Christine] Yeah, let's do that.
-Yes!

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:44.000
-Let's see it.
-Wow.

00:09:44.084 --> 00:09:46.377
This is sick. It's amazing.

00:09:46.461 --> 00:09:48.963
-[Maya] Wow.
-[Mary] These are the best views in LA.

00:09:49.047 --> 00:09:50.590
[Chrishell] On top of the world.

00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:52.592
[Jason] And you get 
the whole Sunset Strip from here.

00:09:52.675 --> 00:09:54.135
In fact, you can even see 
our office right there.

00:09:54.219 --> 00:09:56.471
It's over 4,000 square feet,
this rooftop deck.

00:09:56.554 --> 00:09:59.808
The largest rooftop deck
of any property ever listed in the Hills.

00:09:59.891 --> 00:10:03.269
[Chrishell] Can you imagine just doing,
"Welcome to my humble abode?"

00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:05.980
[Jason] There's nothing humble 
about this, but yeah.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:11.402
All right, find people who are worth
at least 250 million dollars,

00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.363
even if they're not looking for a house.

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.323
The house will sell itself,
just get 'em up here.

00:10:15.406 --> 00:10:17.450
-All right, let's sell this, guys.
-All right, let's go.

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:18.910
Bring it in, team!

00:10:18.993 --> 00:10:20.662
-[all cheer]
-All right!

00:10:20.745 --> 00:10:22.705
[Christine] Those glasses are dope as...
by the way.

